### The box `?` opens over the screen: every key, and every order typed after `:`.
### What is typed is not here and is never translated; only what it does is.

screen-draw-keys-title = keys
screen-draw-keys-close = any key closes this
screen-draw-keys-typed-after = typed after :

screen-draw-keys-leave = leave; the node stops
screen-draw-keys-say = say one of the 333
screen-draw-keys-order = type an order
screen-draw-keys-these = these keys
screen-draw-keys-ping = one heartbeat with a node
screen-draw-keys-join = be handed the file
screen-draw-keys-bootstrap = begin a line of your own
screen-draw-keys-tor = onion address up or down
screen-draw-keys-bridge = add a bridge for Tor
screen-draw-keys-helper = the program a bridge needs
screen-draw-keys-status = what this node holds
screen-draw-keys-quit = the same as q
